# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Development Rules

> **Read and follow all rules in AGENTS.md at the project root.** It contains mandatory security constraints for database, API, and infrastructure code.

## Security Quick Reference

- MUST check auth on every endpoint: `if (!c.get('user')) return c.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, 401)`
- MUST validate all input with Zod schemas before processing
- MUST run user-facing queries through `withUserDb(user.id, (tx) => ...)` from `src/server/db/client.ts` (runs as role `app_user`, RLS applies). `adminDb` bypasses RLS: only in the files `tests/structural/db-access-census.test.ts` allows, and only after checking the caller may touch the rows
- MUST enable RLS on every new table, with policies `TO app_user` reading `(SELECT app.user_id())`, and a `WITH CHECK` mirroring `USING` on every write policy
- NEVER build SQL text from input: use Drizzle's query builder or the `sql` template (bound parameters), never `sql.raw()` with user input
- MUST log database errors as `dbErrorForLog(err)`, never `err.message` (it carries the SQL and bound values)
- MUST use `createAuthClient()` for `signInWithPassword()` — never the `supabaseAdmin` singleton
- NEVER return raw database errors to clients
- NEVER expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` to the client

## Stack
- Frontend: React 19, Vite, React Router, TanStack Query, Shadcn UI, Launch UI, Tailwind CSS v4
- Backend: Hono (Node.js), Pino logger, Zod validation
- Database: PostgreSQL via Drizzle ORM (`src/server/db/`), RLS on every table
- Auth: In-process auth in the API server (Better Auth, `src/server/auth/`)
- Tooling: Biome (lint/format), TypeScript, esbuild, Vitest

## Commands
- `npm run dev:start` - Full cold start (Docker + migrations + dev servers)
- `npm run dev` - Start API and Vite dev servers
- `npm run build` - Build client and server
- `npm run lint` - Biome linting
- `npm run typecheck` - TypeScript checking
- `npm test` - Run vitest tests
- `npm run db:migrate` - Run SQL migrations

## Path Aliases
- `@/*` → `src/client/*`
- `@shared/*` → `src/shared/*`
- Never use `@/shared/*` - it won't resolve

## Key Patterns

### Database access
- The browser never queries the database: it calls `/api/v1` routes (via `apiJson` in `src/client/lib/api.ts`)
- Server: `withUserDb(userId | null, fn)` for anything done for a user or anonymous visitor (default); `adminDb` for webhooks, admin tools, jobs (bypasses RLS)
- New table: migration in `supabase/migrations/` (RLS + policies in the same file), then its Drizzle definition in `src/server/db/schema.ts`
- Use `(SELECT app.user_id())` in RLS policies (not bare `app.user_id()`), so it is evaluated once per statement

### Supabase (Auth only)
- Client-side (`src/client/lib/supabase.ts`): sign-in and session only
- Server-side (`src/server/lib/supabase.ts`): `supabaseAdmin.auth.admin.*` for user management; never `.from()`
- Auth is handled by Supabase - don't implement custom auth

### API Routes
- Create in `src/server/routes/v1/`, mount in `src/server/index.ts`
- Validate input with Zod schemas
- Get user via `c.get('user')`, query via `withUserDb(user.id, (tx) => ...)`

### React Pages
- Protected pages: wrap with `<ProtectedRoute>` in `App.tsx`
- Admin pages: wrap with `<SuperAdminProtectedRoute>`
- App pages use `<SidebarProvider>` + `<AppSidebar />` + `<SidebarInset>` layout

### UI
- **Two design libraries**: Shadcn UI primitives (`src/client/components/ui/`) for interface elements; Launch UI blocks (MIT, vendored copy/paste; retinted to the OKLCH palette) for marketing/landing sections. Build custom only when neither fits — and comment why.
- Shadcn UI components in `src/client/components/ui/`
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Use `toast` from `sonner` for notifications
- Button `asChild` with Link children: add `className="inline-flex items-center gap-2"` to the Link, `shrink-0` on icons

### Data Fetching
- **NEVER use raw `fetch` in `useEffect`** — always use `useQuery` for reads, `useMutation` for writes. Raw fetch bypasses deduplication/caching and React StrictMode will double-fire it.
- **Gate authenticated queries** with `enabled: !!user` to prevent 401s for logged-out users
- **Use `getAuthHeaders()`** from `@/lib/api.ts` — never duplicate it locally, never send empty `Authorization` headers
- Shared hooks in `src/client/hooks/api/`
- Invalidate related queries after mutations: `queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['items'] })`

### Database (migrations)
- Migrations in `supabase/migrations/` with incrementing prefix
- Always enable RLS on new tables
- Helper functions: `get_user_org_ids()`, `get_user_admin_org_ids()`, `is_super_admin()`

### Environment Variables
- Server env vars validated in `src/server/lib/env.ts`
- Client env vars must start with `VITE_`
- Feature flags use `isXConfigured()` pattern
